 Only known parser diagnostics are ordinary rejection; unexpected exceptions stay findings.\n\nThe adapters use actual package entry points. PE validates metadata before Inspector/loadAssembly and caps rows/method bytes; bytecode checks expansion/depth before deserialization and executes only a single scalar method with 1,024 instructions, one frame, 4 KiB stack and 8 KiB managed heap; PDB applies reader budgets; ZIP caps entries, paths and decoded bytes. Inputs are at most 64 KiB. No external corpus, network access, extraction, dependencies or production-package changes.\n\n## Validation\n\n26/26 focused tests passed without skips at local `a73dbc51`, tree `a8c1d9ac0477182c778965426cd6ed58f3884e36`, using Node 24.19.0 / npm 11.9.0 / Linux x64. Command:\n\n`node scripts/limited.js node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-reporter=tap tests/conformance/fuzz/binary-targets.test.js`\n\nThe suite checks real valid/deterministic seeds, input ownership, cancellation, metadata and size limits, scalar instruction budgets, unsupported execution profiles, PDB references, ZIP validation and unknown exception preservation. Static read-only review and whitespace checks completed. Required hosted core will qualify the published tree. The GitHub connector assigned commit metadata after verifying the remote tree matches the tested tree.\n\n## Remaining acceptance\n\n- The requested ten-minute PE campaign and cross-platform captures remain pending.\n- Verified bytecode outside the documented scalar profile returns unsupported; this is not full arbitrary-image VM fuzz qualification.\n- Portable PDB uses owned small seeds, not the entire external fixture corpus.\n- ZIP remains in memory; workspace import, filesystem extraction and bomb campaigns are not qualified.\n- Existing `deserializeImage('null')` and embedded-PDB compression error taxonomy are preserved as potential findings, not hidden by generic error catches.\n\nThe fixed process harness and serial campaign workflow follow in 